      "id": 154091,
      "name": "dshields",
      "username": "dshields",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/dshields/{size}/1968_2.png",
      "created_at": "2016-02-06T19:32:51.000Z",
      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"Trajector\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/trajector/48/1914_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Trajector:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Thank you! Most of my skill comes from practice - you could definitely get there. <img src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/images/emoji/apple/slight_smile.png?v=12\" title=\":slight_smile:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":slight_smile:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\"> The trickiest aspect is plotting things out beforehand, to make sure that I fit everything into the map. (Lots of people over on the Cartographers' Guild use GIMP or Photoshop, and so can move objects around after the fact. I made that harder on myself by drawing by hand.)</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Now I may be able to do something in photoshop, but not by hand, even my stick figures look bad LOL. But it is good work. and it looks more Real, like something they would pull out of thier bag.</p>",
